  message: "Flipped violated→satisfied (owner convergence call 2026-07-17: 'add the mainstream shape_id guard, then flip'). BEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE (closure-evidence discipline): (1) DEEP cross-language cohort CLEAN — session deep-20260717-200119, 8 repos spanning ts/js/go/php/python/csharp/java/swift/c/rust: ZERO new parity gaps in the emission-parity matrix's semantic-field columns; csharp shape_id 0→100% of shapeable (105/105) after PR #704; the two low cells (csharp docstring 0%, js is_exported 0.2%) verified LEGITIMATE (source has no doc comments; pre-existing CommonJS texture), not analyzer gaps. (2) The standing ratchet tests/test_emission_parity_matrix.py is GREEN at 88 passed — now including a shape_id hard-lock column (PR #713) that closes the identity-field blind spot which had let the csharp regression reach a bakeoff before any standing test caught it. (3) The semantic-field parity this META governs (signature/qualified_name/is_exported/docstring/complexity/edge_calls/edge_imports/emits_variable/emits_field) is fully locked across the 8 core analyzers; all named children satisfied/done/wont_do (INV-golap/loguk/gilok/gojit, WI-fagab, WI-bujot). SCOPE: shape_id is spec-optional (spec §6, ~41/70 analyzers) — the ADR/spec/gate all present it as coverage-scoped, NOT a uniform contract — so the niche solidity/wgsl 'without'-bucket shape_id gaps are documented coverage-completeness work (WI-lutob), not INV-jahiv violations. Advance-not-block: WI-hudug (P3, per-kind qualified_name writer-contract entry) hardens but does not gate. Basis: 3-lens ADR/spec/consumer investigation 2026-07-17."  # aa44
